Recently, some Gentleman from the UK posted a program that reversed
the lines in a file. I figured that I should post this somewhat 
shorter solution.

----cute here, huh?----
/*
 * mirror the recursive way
 *
 */

#include <stdio.h>

main() {
    char	foo[BUFSIZ];

    if(gets(foo) == NULL) return;
    main();
    puts(foo);
}
